message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Scale-Optimized Geometric Acceleration of Polygonal Approximations to π"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: C. Wayne
date-released: 2026-05-09
version: revised-preprint-v1
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22819869"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/scale-optimized-polygonal-pi-acceleration"
url: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/scale-optimized-polygonal-pi-acceleration"
abstract: >-
  A scale-b Richardson-Lagrange acceleration framework for polygonal
  approximations to pi, with uniform geometric-node weight stability,
  explicit analytic remainder bounds, high-precision slope verification,
  and a precise separation between dyadic constructibility and approximate
  tripling architectures.
keywords:
  - polygonal approximation
  - pi
  - N-series
  - Richardson extrapolation
  - geometric nodes
  - q-Pochhammer
  - constructible geometry
